---
import data from '../data/events.json';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>About — Indian Dance NYC</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <p><a href={`${base}/`}>← Back to the calendar</a></p>
      <h1>About</h1>

      <p>
        Indian dance in New York is listed in two places that never overlap.
        Community listings carry the festivals and the recitals. The big
        presenters book world-class Indian artists and file them under "dance."
        Neither knows about the other. Ten events in a year, ten venues, no
        single list.
      </p>

      <p>This is the single list.</p>

      <h2>What's here</h2>
      <p>
        Indian classical and semi-classical dance across the New York City metro
        area — Bharatanatyam, Kathak, Odissi, Kuchipudi, Mohiniyattam, Manipuri,
        Sattriya, Kathakali — plus folk, Bollywood and Indian fusion, and dance
        talks and workshops. Five boroughs, New Jersey, Long Island,
        Westchester. Music-only concerts are out of scope.
      </p>

      <h2>How it stays current</h2>
      <p>
        Automated sweeps read {data.sourceCount} venue calendars and listings
        three times a week, plus a weekly search for events beyond them. Every
        event is link-checked before it appears and re-checked afterwards.
        Nothing is listed on a maybe. Past events stay up for six months so you
        can see what you missed.
      </p>

      <p class="fine">
        The venue's own page is always the authority on dates, prices and
        tickets. Add the whole calendar to Google or Apple Calendar with the
        <a href={`${base}/calendar.ics`}>calendar feed</a>.
      </p>
    </main>
    <style is:global>
      :root {
        --bg: #faf7f2; --ink: #2b2118; --muted: #7a6a5c; --accent: #b3512f; --line: #e8dfd3;
      }
      @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
        :root { --bg: #191411; --ink: #f0e7dc; --muted: #a89a8a; --accent: #e07a4f; --line: #3a3129; }
      }
      body { margin: 0; background: var(--bg); color: var(--ink); font: 16px/1.6 system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif; }
      main { max-width: 640px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2.5rem 1.25rem 4rem; }
      h1 { font-family: Georgia, serif; letter-spacing: -.02em; }
      h2 { font-family: Georgia, serif; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-top: 1.8rem; }
      a { color: var(--accent); }
      .fine { color: var(--muted); font-size: .9rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding-top: 1rem; margin-top: 2.5rem; }
    </style>
  </body>
</html>
